# Thinkers maps — bias correction

Add/revise thinkers, currents, timeline nodes, SVGs, glossaries → correct **male** + **European** skew. Western male canon not unmarked default.

## Required checks before shipping a change

1. **Census** — after edits, rough count named women vs person/cluster nodes; note non-European / Global South. Change adds men only → add/propose matching women and/or non-European interlocutors on same current.
2. **Placement** — figures *inside* argument (edges, prose hinges, currents tags), not segregated “diversity” sidebar / afterthought band.
3. **Entry points** — male/Europe-heavy spine → early non-European or woman hinge (e.g. Fanon beside Sartre; Federici/Firestone inside Freudo-Marxism; Hui/Merchant/Hayles on techne).
4. **Honesty** — frame notes / currents may state imbalance; no fake parity. No erase European archives — thicken + rebalance.
5. **Currents** (`map-currents.js`) — new thinkers get right cohort tags; create/widen current, not timeline-only.

## Good vs bad

```text
❌ BAD — add three more Frankfurt/Warwick men; leave sex ratio and geography unremarked
✅ GOOD — same addition paired with a woman or decolonial interlocutor on that quarrel, wired in prose + timeline + current

❌ BAD — park all non-European names on a separate “other” page only
✅ GOOD — colonial / feminist / cosmotechnics pressure sits on the map that asks the question
```

## Scope

Grounding, Genealogies, Constellations, Technics, Thinkers Timeline, browse-by-current, Fiction of the maps, booklet assembly of those pages.
